# Changelog

Notable changes to Tupista. Format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com);
versioning follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org).

Everything so far is pre-release: there are no users yet, so it all sits under
Unreleased until the first Avalonia desktop build ships. Entries here describe
what changed for someone USING the engine — internal refactors belong in the
git history, not in this file.

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- `Board` value type with an 81-character import/export format, and validation
  of duplicate digits in rows, columns and boxes.
- Backtracking solver and a capped `countSolutions`, giving ground truth and a
  uniqueness check.
- Human technique ladder, tiers 1-7: singles, pointing/claiming, naked and
  hidden pairs and triples, X-Wing, XY-Wing, XY-Chain. Difficulty is reported
  as the hardest tier required; puzzles beyond the ladder report as such.
- `nextHint`: one next human step, with the chain of enabling eliminations that
  makes it true from the player's own view of the board, at three disclosure
  levels (vague, mechanism, full).
- Hint chains are pruned to the deductions a placement genuinely depends on,
  rather than everything the engine happened to try along the way.
- Pencil marks on cells, and `auditPencilMarks` reporting marks that are
  missing or that later placements have made stale. Marks are never used for
  solving.
- C ABI (`core/capi`, `tupista.h`) for host applications, built both as a
  shared library for desktop and a static library for iOS.
